DOCUMENT();        # This should be the first executable line in the problem.

loadMacros(
"PG.pl",
"PGbasicmacros.pl",
"PGchoicemacros.pl",
"PGanswermacros.pl",
"PGgraphmacros.pl",
"PGnumericalmacros.pl",
"PGstatisticsmacros.pl",
"PGauxiliaryFunctions.pl"
);

TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;

$a = random(2,6,1);
$b = non_zero_random(-5,5,1);

## 1 and sqrt(3)(1-2x) is an orthonormal basis for the subspace. Let i(x)=sqrt(3)(1-2x).
## prod_fh = $a/3 + $b; 
## prod_fi = - $a*sqrt(3)/6;

$proj = "- $a/6 + $b + $a x";

BEGIN_TEXT

The pairing below defines an the inner product in \( C[0,1] \), the vector space of all continuous functions on the domain \([0,1]\).
\[ \langle f,g \rangle = \int_0^1 f(x)g(x)dx \]
Compute the orthogonal projection of \(f(x) = $a x^2 + $b \) onto the subspace \( W \) spanned by \( g(x) = x \) and 
\( h(x) = 1 \). 
$PAR
(Caution: \( g\) and \(h\) do not form an orthogonal basis of \( W \).)
$PAR
\( \operatorname{proj}_W(f) = \) \{ans_rule(20)\}. 

END_TEXT

ANS(fun_cmp($proj));

ENDDOCUMENT();       # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
